<title>USA: DCR rates El Salvador foreign currency Double-B.</title>
<headline>DCR rates El Salvador foreign currency Double-B.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Monday it assigned a rating of Double-B to El Salvador's foreign currency obligations.</p>
<p>The country's good fundamental macroeconomic conditions support the rating, Duff &amp; Phelps said, citing a stable exchange rate, reduced inflation and increased growth.</p>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps said it also rated El Salvador's short-term obligations D-Four, its long-term local currency Single-A-minus, and its short-term local currency D-Two.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
